  "why": "Since Protocol 23 (CAP-67) the native asset contract emits transaction-level fee events: one with stage BEFORE_ALL_TXS that charges the full fee, and for a Soroban transaction one with stage AFTER_ALL_TXS whose amount is negative, the refund. Readers that treat every fee event as a charge, that take the absolute value, or that read only operation events, report the wrong fee or none. The focus is a native-asset approve, which moves no value and leaves the fee events as the only movements.",
